OL,3,GNEWSAToddler's 'second chance at life'
OL,4,Aafter stem cell transplant
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn 18-month-old boy with a rare blood
OL,7,Fcondition has been given "a second
OL,8,Fchance at life" after undergoing a
OL,9,Flife-saving stem cell transplant, his
OL,10,Fmum has said.
OL,12,FRonnie, from Wirral on Merseyside, was
OL,13,Fdiagnosed with aplastic anaemia - which
OL,14,Fis fatal if left untreated - a week
OL,15,Fbefore his first birthday in March last
OL,16,Fyear.
OL,18,FHe underwent the transplant after a
OL,19,Fsuitable anonymous match was found in
OL,20,Fthe US, with Ronnie's mum Laura saying:
OL,21,F"I can't describe the feeling of what
OL,22,Fthe donor did for our little boy."
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,406,400,260,160,0,100
